diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..2209037 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,12 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## On-device article translation
+
+Use the translation bar above news content to choose a reading language and select **Translate**. It translates headlines, teasers, article bodies, and captions on the current page. **Show original** restores the English text and can cancel a pending translation. Switching target languages always translates from the original English to avoid accumulating translation errors.
+
+Translation uses the browser's [Translator API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/translator-api) in a secure context. Support and available language pairs depend on the browser and device. The control checks availability and shows language-pack download progress; it explains when translation is unavailable. Article text is never sent to a translation service. Navigation starts with original content and a fresh control. Formatting and links are preserved, and code, scripts, bylines, and site navigation are excluded.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
